            <h2 class="section-title">How We Work</h2>
            <ul class="why-list">
              <li class="why-item"><span class="why-dot"></span><div><strong>Assessment</strong><p>Every health care engagement starts with a free on-site assessment. We'll look at the tree, discuss what you've observed, and explain what we're seeing.</p></div></li>
              <li class="why-item"><span class="why-dot"></span><div><strong>Diagnosis</strong><p>We assess the tree's condition — looking at leaves, bark, structure, and soil. Many issues have visible signs; some require samples and lab analysis.</p></div></li>
              <li class="why-item"><span class="why-dot"></span><div><strong>Treatment Plan</strong><p>Once we understand the problem, we create a treatment plan with realistic expectations. We explain what's likely to work, what will take time, and what the costs are.</p></div></li>
              <li class="why-item"><span class="why-dot"></span><div><strong>Follow-Up</strong><p>Tree health is an ongoing relationship. We check progress, adjust treatments, and help you establish a care routine that keeps your trees healthy over the long term.</p></div></li>
