    <section class="faq-section">
      <div class="section-container">
        <div class="section-header">
          <p class="section-label">Common Questions</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Tree Health Care FAQ</h2>
          <p class="section-desc">Answers to questions from Eau Claire homeowners about tree health and treatment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item" open>
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question-text">How do I know if my tree needs health care?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Signs of trouble include unusual leaf discoloration, premature leaf drop, bark damage or peeling, dead branches in the crown, fungal growth on the trunk or roots, and visibly stressed foliage. If something looks off, call us for an assessment — early detection matters.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question-text">Can you treat emerald ash borer or other pest infestations?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>We can help with pest identification and, in some cases, treatment options. Emerald ash borer is particularly challenging — preventive treatment is most effective before infestation. Call us to assess your ash trees and discuss your options.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question-text">What does tree fertilization cost?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Cost depends on tree size, number of trees, and the type of treatment needed. We provide a free assessment and give you an honest estimate before any work begins.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question-text">Is treatment always successful?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Not always. Some tree health problems are too advanced by the time they're discovered. We give you honest assessments and won't sell you treatments that are unlikely to help. When a tree can't be saved, we explain that too.</p></div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

